  the existing `moveRect` pure function; shift+arrow keys resize via
  the existing `resizeRect` pure function. Convention chosen (not
  specified by the PRD, documented here for future consistency):
  shift+Right/Down grow the rect (via the `e`/`s` handles), shift+
  Left/Up shrink it. All keyboard math reuses the exact same
  display-to-natural coordinate pipeline as pointer dragging
  (`toDisplayRect` -> `moveRect`/`resizeRect` -> `toNaturalRect` ->
  `#layout()` -> emit `change`), so no new coordinate-mapping code
  was needed -- this validates the US-005 design decision to
  centralize that math in pure functions.
- `e.preventDefault()` on handled arrow keys stops the page from
  scrolling while the crop rect has focus.
- Added a `:focus-visible` outline on `.crop-rect` in `src/index.css`
  reusing the existing `--image-crop-focus-color` variable (already
  added in US-004 anticipating this story).
