## 2026-07-24 - DT-002

- DT-001 already produced the `<label class="picker"><input/></label>`
  markup, so the click/keyboard-opens-the-picker mechanics were already
  correct for free (native label semantics -- no JS click forwarding,
  no tabindex/role needed). The real gap was DT-002's other criterion:
  "clicking the box while an image is showing reopens the picker and
  replaces the image", which needs the picker to visually overlap the
  preview image once one is loaded, per the task doc's "Layering"
  section (also restated verbatim in DT-002's own `notes` field, which
  is what pointed at the mechanism).
- Implemented that layering, scoped tightly to what DT-002's
  acceptance criteria require (not the fuller DT-007/DT-008 box-sizing
  work, which is out of scope this session):
  - `src/index.ts`: `#setFile` now also adds `has-image` to `.box`
    (previously only `.preview` got it); `#clear` removes it from both.
  - `src/index.css`: `.box.has-image .picker { position: absolute;
    inset: 0 }` makes the label overlay the whole box once an image is
    showing. `.preview` gained `pointer-events: none` so a click on the
    `<img>` falls through to the label underneath (`.overlay > *`
    already had `pointer-events: auto` from US-001, so the ALT/edit/
    remove buttons -- which paint after the label in DOM order -- stay
    clickable and do NOT reach the input). Also added `.box:has(input
    :focus-visible)` with the existing `--image-input-focus-color`
    variable for the visible focus ring criterion.
  - Did NOT touch box sizing/prompt content (`.picker` in the *empty*
    state still collapses to zero size, since it has no in-flow
    content until DT-008 adds the icon/prompt-text markup and DT-007/
    DT-010 add the in-flow-vs-absolute toggle for that state) -- this
    matches DT-001's/DT-007's own notes and is explicitly deferred.
- Wrote failing tests first in `test/index.ts` (confirmed 1 failing
  assertion -- `#setFile adds has-image to .box` -- before the fix; the
  other new tests around label-click and overlay-buttons-don't-open
  already passed against the DT-001 markup, since those were pre-
  existing native-semantics guarantees, not new behavior):
  1. the picker has no `tabindex`/`role` attributes,
  2. clicking the `.picker` label forwards a click to the input,
  3. `#setFile`/`#clear` toggle `has-image` on `.box`,
  4. clicking ALT/edit/remove does not fire a click on the input.
- **Could not test the CSS-dependent click-passthrough
  (`.box.has-image .picker` overlay) via `npm test`**, per the
  existing Codebase Patterns note: `test/index.html` does not load
  `src/index.css`. Verified it instead with the Playwright MCP tools
  against `npm run start`: uploaded a 400x300 test PNG via a real file
  chooser (triggered with `input.click()` + `browser_file_upload`,
  since Playwright's ref-based click on the input itself fails --
  the input's own hit-test area is clipped to nothing by `clip-path:
  inset(50%)`, which is expected; real users click the label, not the
  input), confirmed `document.elementFromPoint` over the image (away
  from the overlay buttons) resolved to `LABEL.picker`, then did a real
  mouse click at that point and confirmed the file chooser reopened.
  Also confirmed clicking the "Add alt text" badge does NOT reopen the
  chooser. Killed the vite dev server and removed the scratch PNGs and
  `.playwright-mcp/` afterwards.
- Files changed: `src/index.ts`, `src/index.css`, `test/index.ts`,
  `specs/drop-target.json` (DT-002 `passes: true`).
- Tests: 4 new tape tests (9 new assertions). Full `npm test` (lint +
  build + typecheck + tape-run) passes with 124 total assertions.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The empty (no-image) box still collapses to zero size in a real
    browser right now (no prompt content yet) -- don't try to
    Playwright-click an empty box's picker/label directly; test that
    path with structural assertions (label wraps input, no tabindex/
    role) instead, and defer real click-position testing on the empty
    box until DT-008 (prompt content) and DT-007/DT-010 (box sizing)
    land.
  - Playwright's ref-based `browser_click` on the file `<input>`
    itself fails once it's hidden via `clip-path: inset(50%)` --
    "element intercepts pointer events" -- because clip-path also
    clips the hit-test region, not just painting. That's correct,
    intended behavior (only the label should be clickable by a mouse
    user), but it means manual verification of this pattern needs
    `input.click()` via `browser_evaluate` (or a real click on the
    label/box coordinates) rather than a direct ref-click on the input.
